<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.3.4">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://anialiu126.github.io/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://anialiu126.github.io/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2026-09-30T14:55:50+00:00</updated><id>https://anialiu126.github.io/feed.xml</id><title type="html">blank</title><subtitle>Anna (Ania) Liu is a gravitational-wave astrophysicist and Postdoctoral Fellow at the Perimeter Institute for Theoretical Physics, working on black-hole ringdown, lensing, and tests of general relativity. </subtitle><entry><title type="html">Postdoctoral Applications Panel Discussion</title><link href="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/postdoc-applications-panel/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Postdoctoral Applications Panel Discussion"/><published>2026-09-21T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-09-21T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/postdoc-applications-panel</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/postdoc-applications-panel/"><![CDATA[<p>I recently joined a panel discussion at <a href="https://perimeterinstitute.ca/">Perimeter Institute</a> on navigating the postdoc application process, alongside David Schmid, Naren Manjunath, and Maya Berger, moderated by Jacqueline Caminiti. We shared our experiences and practical advice on finding positions, preparing research statements, securing recommendation letters, networking, interviews, and choosing between offers. We also discussed how to manage the uncertainty of application season while keeping up with research.</p> <p>🎥 <a href="https://pirsa.org/26090051">Watch the recording on PIRSA</a> (DOI <a href="https://doi.org/10.48660/26090051">10.48660/26090051</a>)</p> <div class="row mt-3"> <div class="col-sm-6 mt-3"> <a href="https://pirsa.org/26090051"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/postdoc-panel-ania-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/postdoc-panel-ania-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/postdoc-panel-ania-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/postdoc-panel-ania.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" alt="Ania speaking during the postdoctoral applications panel at Perimeter Institute" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </a> </div> <div class="col-sm-6 mt-3"> <a href="https://pirsa.org/26090051"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/postdoc-panel-still-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/postdoc-panel-still-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/postdoc-panel-still-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/postdoc-panel-still.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" alt="Postdoctoral applications panel discussion at Perimeter Institute" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </a> </div> </div>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="talks"/><category term="career"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A panel discussion on postdoc applications at the Perimeter Institute]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Cosmic Fossils: Science Podcast with Rakiura</title><link href="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/cosmic-fossils-podcast/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Cosmic Fossils: Science Podcast with Rakiura"/><published>2026-09-15T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-09-15T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/cosmic-fossils-podcast</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/cosmic-fossils-podcast/"><![CDATA[<p><a href="https://www.instagram.com/rakiuralabs/reel/Dbp2-ZAujV5/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="scicomm-reel"> <img src="/assets/img/scicomm-reel.jpg?1eab8ef2da120f49e2bf11f555780768" alt="Anna Liu introducing gravitational-wave paleontology in a Rakiura Labs video" decoding="async"/> <span>🎥 Watch on Instagram</span> </a></p> <p>I recently recorded two episodes of <em>Cosmic Fossils</em>, the podcast of the Gravitational-Wave Paleontology Lab at <a href="https://www.rakiura.co/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rakiura</a>. In the series, we follow massive stars from birth to their explosive deaths, and explore how the gravitational waves from the black holes they leave behind help us read the history of the Universe.</p> <ul> <li><strong>S1E1: The Dinosaurs of the Universe</strong>  ·  <a href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/24hqp2TKzNzFyLp3wPrLFz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Spotify</a> · <a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/s1e1-the-dinosaurs-of-the-universe/id6811229846?i=1000789115180" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple Podcasts</a> · <a href="https://www.rakiura.co/labs/gw-paleontology/series/cosmic-fossils" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rakiura</a></li> <li><strong>S1E2: We Are Made of Exploded Massive Star Dust</strong>  ·  <a href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/7wtYHCGIsyTLoElOQuXxaS" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Spotify</a> · <a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/s1e2-we-are-made-of-exploded-massive-star-dust/id6811229846?i=1000789788185" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple Podcasts</a> · <a href="https://www.rakiura.co/labs/gw-paleontology/series/cosmic-fossils" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rakiura</a></li> </ul> <p>🎙️ Listen on <a href="https://open.spotify.com/show/5h74Xcz0TDQHvSscUhp9sG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Spotify</a>, <a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/cosmic-fossils/id6811229846" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple Podcasts</a> or <a href="https://www.rakiura.co/labs/gw-paleontology/series/cosmic-fossils" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rakiura</a>.</p> <div class="row mt-4" style="clear: both"> <div class="col-sm mt-3"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/cosmic-fossils-pillars-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/cosmic-fossils-pillars-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/cosmic-fossils-pillars-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/cosmic-fossils-pillars.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" alt="The Pillars of Creation in the Eagle Nebula, imaged by the Hubble Space Telescope" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> </div> <div class="caption"> The Pillars of Creation in the Eagle Nebula, a nursery where new stars are born. Image: NASA, ESA and the Hubble Heritage Team (STScI/AURA), public domain. </div> <p>More about this work on my <a href="/science-communication/">Science Communication</a> page.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="outreach"/><category term="science-communication"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Two podcast episodes on massive stars and gravitational-wave paleontology]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Seminar at the Perimeter Institute</title><link href="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/perimeter-institute-seminar/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Seminar at the Perimeter Institute"/><published>2026-06-18T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-06-18T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/perimeter-institute-seminar</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/perimeter-institute-seminar/"><![CDATA[<p>I gave a seminar at the <a href="https://perimeterinstitute.ca/">Perimeter Institute for Theoretical Physics</a>, presenting my work on gravitational-wave lensing. A recording is available via <a href="https://doi.org/10.48660/26060068">PIRSA (DOI 10.48660/26060068)</a>.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="talks"/><category term="lensing"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A seminar at the Perimeter Institute for Theoretical Physics]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">LVK GWTC-4 Lensing Webinar</title><link href="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/lvk-gwtc4-lensing-webinar/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="LVK GWTC-4 Lensing Webinar"/><published>2026-04-23T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-04-23T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/lvk-gwtc4-lensing-webinar</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/lvk-gwtc4-lensing-webinar/"><![CDATA[<p>Together with collaborators, I presented the latest results from the LIGO–Virgo–KAGRA GWTC-4 search for gravitational-wave lensing signatures, in an online webinar streamed live on <a href="https://youtu.be/A7_nQeAob2E?si=ZOjPl-io6b7tNlWV">YouTube</a>.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="talks"/><category term="lensing"/><category term="LVK"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Presenting the GWTC-4 search for gravitational-wave lensing signatures]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">GWnext Meeting 2026, Beijing</title><link href="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/gwnext-meeting-beijing/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="GWnext Meeting 2026, Beijing"/><published>2026-03-05T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-03-05T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/gwnext-meeting-beijing</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2026/gwnext-meeting-beijing/"><![CDATA[<p>I gave an invited talk, “Extracting physics from gravitational waves: parameter estimation and waveform modelling”, at the <a href="https://aletorreso.wixsite.com/atogw/gwnext2026">GWnext 2026 Meeting</a>, held at the Beijing Institute of Mathematical Sciences and Applications (BIMSA) on 2–6 March 2026. GWnext is a series of meetings on gravitational-wave physics from young researchers for young researchers, bringing together theory, astrophysics, and detection. My talk covered recent developments and challenges in the data analysis of gravitational-wave signals from the LIGO–Virgo–KAGRA Collaboration.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="talks"/><category term="LVK"/><category term="data-analysis"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Invited talk at the GWnext 2026 Meeting in Beijing, China]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Academic visits in Beijing</title><link href="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2025/academic_visits_Beijing/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Academic visits in Beijing"/><published>2025-07-05T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-07-05T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2025/academic_visits_Beijing</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2025/academic_visits_Beijing/"><![CDATA[<p>I recently spent some time in Beijing visiting several gravitational-wave groups — at Beijing Normal University, Tsinghua University, Peking University, and the National Astronomical Observatory of the Chinese Academy of Sciences 🌌 It was a great opportunity to dive into their latest research, exchange ideas, share some of my own work, and enjoy the beautiful campuses 🌿✨</p> <div class="row mt-3"> <div class="col-sm-6 mt-3"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/Tsinghua_25-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/Tsinghua_25-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/Tsinghua_25-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/Tsinghua_25.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <div class="col-sm-6 mt-3"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/BNU_25-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/BNU_25-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/BNU_25-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/BNU_25.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <div class="col-sm-6 mt-3"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/PKU_KIAA-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/PKU_KIAA-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/PKU_KIAA-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/PKU_KIAA.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <div class="col-sm-6 mt-3"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/PKU_campus-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/PKU_campus-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/PKU_campus-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/PKU_campus.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> </div>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="academic"/><category term="visit"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Visiting GW groups in Beijing]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">London–Oldenburg Relativity Seminar</title><link href="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2025/london-oldenburg-relativity-seminar/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="London–Oldenburg Relativity Seminar"/><published>2025-06-05T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-06-05T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2025/london-oldenburg-relativity-seminar</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2025/london-oldenburg-relativity-seminar/"><![CDATA[<p>I was invited to speak at the online London–Oldenburg Relativity Seminar, where I presented my research on gravitational-wave lensing.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="talks"/><category term="lensing"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Invited online talk at the London–Oldenburg Relativity Seminar]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">I defended my PhD! 🎓🥳</title><link href="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2025/phd_defense/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="I defended my PhD! 🎓🥳"/><published>2025-06-02T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-06-02T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2025/phd_defense</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2025/phd_defense/"><![CDATA[<p>On June 2, 2025, I officially defended my PhD at the Chinese University of Hong Kong 🎓🥳</p> <div class="row mt-3"> <div class="col-sm-4 mt-3"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/defense_main-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/defense_main-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/defense_main-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/defense_main.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <div class="col-sm-4 mt-3"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/defense_2-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/defense_2-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/defense_2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/defense_2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <div class="col-sm-4 mt-3"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/defense_last-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/defense_last-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/defense_last-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/defense_last.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> </div> <p>It’s been a long, challenging, but also incredibly rewarding journey. I couldn’t have made it to the final chapter without the kindness, encouragement, and support of so many amazing people ✨</p> <p>Huge thanks to my fellow group members of the <a href="https://gw.phy.cuhk.edu.hk/people/">GW group at CUHK</a>, who have become my academic family over the past 4 years. I am also grateful to my committee members — Prof. Paul Lasky, Prof. Ming Chung Chu, and Prof. Kenny Ng — as well as my supervisors, Prof. Tjonnie Li and Prof. Otto Hannuksela, for their guidance and support during this key milestone of my PhD journey.</p> <p>Now onto the next adventure!🚀</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="phd"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[I defended my PhD at the Chinese University of Hong Kong.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">GWPAW 2024</title><link href="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2024/distill/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="GWPAW 2024"/><published>2024-06-01T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2024-06-01T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2024/distill</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2024/distill/"><![CDATA[<h2 id="black-hole-archaeology">Black hole archaeology</h2> <p>In May 2024 I attended the <a href="https://www.gwpaw2024.space/">GWPAW</a> in Birmingham and gave a contributed talk “Birth Kick Estimates of Second-Generation Black Holes Observed By LIGO-Virgo: Implications for Formation Channels and Host Environments”.</p> <div class="row mt-3"> <div class="col-sm mt-3 mt-md-0"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/unnamed-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/unnamed-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/unnamed-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/unnamed.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" title="GWPAW talk" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> </div> <div class="row"> <div class="col-sm mt-3 mt-md-0"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/hierarchical_merger-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/hierarchical_merger-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/hierarchical_merger-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/hierarchical_merger.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" title="hierarchical formation" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> </div>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="conferences"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Gravitational Wave Physics and Astronomy Workshop 2024]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">LIGO-Virgo-KAGRA Meeting in Toyama, Japan</title><link href="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2023/LVK_meeting_Toyama/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="LIGO-Virgo-KAGRA Meeting in Toyama, Japan"/><published>2023-10-01T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2023-10-01T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2023/LVK_meeting_Toyama</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://anialiu126.github.io/blog/2023/LVK_meeting_Toyama/"><![CDATA[<p>I attended the LIGO-Virgo-KAGRA (LVK) Collaboration Meeting in Toyama, Japan, which was an inspiring experience. Presenting my poster on gravitational wave lensing sparked meaningful discussions and gave me valuable insights to refine my research. Visiting the KAGRA detector was a highlight—seeing its advanced underground setup and learning about its cryogenic technology was fascinating. This trip deepened my appreciation for the engineering behind gravitational wave detections and the collaborative effort driving the field forward.</p> <div class="row mt-3"> <div class="col-sm-4 mt-3"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/IMG_5095-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/IMG_5095-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/IMG_5095-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/IMG_5095.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <div class="col-sm-4 mt-3"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/IMG_4901-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/IMG_4901-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/IMG_4901-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/IMG_4901.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> <div class="col-sm-4 mt-3"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/IMG_1778.JPG" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/IMG_1778.JPG" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </div> </div>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="conferences"/><category term="LVK"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[The LVK September Meeting and visit to KAGRA]]></summary></entry></feed>